        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(feishu): cap sender-name and streaming token caches",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes two unbounded in-process Maps in the Feishu plugin:\n\n1. **`senderNameCache`** — sender display name lookups with no eviction under high message volume.\n2. **`tokenCache`** — streaming-card tenant access token cache with no eviction.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nApplies `pruneMapToMaxSize` after each cache write: sender names capped at **500**, streaming tokens at **256**, both with LRU eviction.\n\n## User Impact\n\nLong-lived Feishu gateways get bounded memory for sender-name and streaming-token caches. Normal workloads below the caps are unchanged.\n\n## Evidence\n\n```bash\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs run \\\n  extensions/feishu/src/bot-sender-name.test.ts \\\n  extensions/feishu/src/streaming-card.test.ts \\\n  --reporter=verbose\n```\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n- **Behavior or issue addressed:** Feishu sender-name and streaming token caches grew without bound.\n- **Real environment tested:** macOS (Darwin arm64), Node.js v22.22.0, local source checkout on branch `fix/feishu-cap-sender-and-token-caches`.\n- **Exact steps or command run after this patch:**\n  1. `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run extensions/feishu/src/bot-sender-name.test.ts extensions/feishu/src/streaming-card.test.ts --reporter=verbose`\n- **Evidence after fix:**\n\n```text\n ✓ evicts oldest sender name cache entries once the cache exceeds its cap\n ✓ evicts oldest streaming token cache entries once the cache exceeds its cap\n\n Test Files  2 passed (2)\n      Tests  25 passed (25)\n```\n\n- **Observed result after fix:** Regression tests exercise production cache helpers and confirm oldest entries are evicted at cap while newest entries remain cached.\n- **What was not tested:** Live Feishu/Lark API token fetch or contact lookup.\n",
        "branch": "fix/feishu-cap-sender-and-token-caches",
